WEBVTT

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:50.760
You'll definitely remember, Kaito!

00:02:02.330 --> 00:02:03.370
Seira!

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:12.120
Seira, I'll definitely get your orange heart shards back!

00:02:13.970 --> 00:02:15.870
The Thing I Want

00:02:21.580 --> 00:02:22.890
Kaito!

00:02:23.570 --> 00:02:25.360
What is it, Lucia?

00:02:25.360 --> 00:02:30.590
Um, Kaito, did you decide to not leave Mikaru's house?

00:02:31.900 --> 00:02:32.470
Yeah.

00:02:35.540 --> 00:02:36.270
I'm sorry.

00:02:37.090 --> 00:02:42.170
I figured that I should be with Mikaru for now.

00:02:42.470 --> 00:02:45.650
I can't leave her alone like that.

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:48.520
I see. I figured as much.

00:02:48.520 --> 00:02:53.210
Mikaru isn't in good health and she needs someone to stay with her.

00:02:54.020 --> 00:02:54.830
I'm sorry.

00:02:55.080 --> 00:02:57.790
Oh no! Don't worry about it.

00:02:58.000 --> 00:02:59.640
I'm perfectly fine with it.

00:02:59.640 --> 00:03:01.780
See you later. Bye bye.

00:03:16.210 --> 00:03:17.180
Kaito!

00:03:22.920 --> 00:03:23.820
Rihito-san!

00:03:23.820 --> 00:03:26.140
Hi there, Lucia-chan.

00:03:38.260 --> 00:03:41.520
Lucia-chan, you seem sad.

00:03:42.820 --> 00:03:44.510
That's not true.

00:03:44.510 --> 00:03:46.960
I'm always cheerful. Cheerful!

00:03:46.960 --> 00:03:49.960
Don't force yourself, Lucia-chan.

00:03:50.740 --> 00:03:53.190
You're really very sad, aren't you?

00:03:58.030 --> 00:03:59.420
It's not good to force yourself.

00:03:59.960 --> 00:04:03.980
When you feel sad, it's better to let yourself cry.

00:04:06.550 --> 00:04:08.610
Huh? That's strange.

00:04:08.740 --> 00:04:12.100
Why are my eyes full of tears? Eh?

00:04:12.680 --> 00:04:18.330
Those tears must be the tears that you tried your best to hold back.

00:04:18.720 --> 00:04:21.110
Don't think about it too much for now. Just cry your heart out.

00:04:21.110 --> 00:04:29.420
If you say that and treat me with such kindness, I won't be able to stop my tears!

00:04:31.410 --> 00:04:34.970
It's okay. Don't think about it and cry your heart out.

00:04:35.320 --> 00:04:36.560
Rihito-san.

00:04:36.800 --> 00:04:40.950
Lucia-chan, cry on me as much as you need to.{Lucia-chan, just cry as much as you need to, on my shoulder.}

00:04:41.440 --> 00:04:43.030
Cry until you have no more tears left.

00:04:56.710 --> 00:05:01.260
The Mermaid Princesses must be in this city somewhere.

00:05:01.890 --> 00:05:06.710
I'll use the power that Mikeru-sama bestowed upon me to draw them out.

00:05:12.360 --> 00:05:14.190
Lucia's really late.

00:05:14.190 --> 00:05:17.390
No kidding. Where did she go?

00:05:17.390 --> 00:05:19.900
Hmm? Someone pulled up.

00:05:20.760 --> 00:05:21.660
Rihito-san.

00:05:21.970 --> 00:05:24.510
I'm sorry for causing you so much trouble today.

00:05:24.510 --> 00:05:25.890
That's all right.

00:05:25.890 --> 00:05:28.850
Lucia let Rihito-san take her home.

00:05:28.850 --> 00:05:30.360
Way to go, Lucia!

00:05:30.360 --> 00:05:34.660
Do you feel a bit better now, Lucia-chan?

00:05:34.660 --> 00:05:38.750
Yeah. Rihito-san, thank you very much.

00:05:38.890 --> 00:05:41.420
Lucia-chan, where would you like to go next time?

00:05:41.420 --> 00:05:42.070
Huh?

00:05:42.540 --> 00:05:46.370
I can take you anywhere you want to go.

00:05:46.370 --> 00:05:49.880
Also, could you let me know if there's something you'd like?

00:05:49.880 --> 00:05:52.700
Something that I'd like?

00:05:52.700 --> 00:05:57.040
I want to give you a present. You don't mind, do you?

00:05:57.040 --> 00:05:59.180
Oh no, I don't mind at all.

00:05:59.180 --> 00:06:01.940
Okay. Go ahead and think about it.

00:06:02.340 --> 00:06:03.190
Good night.

00:06:03.670 --> 00:06:04.400
Good night.

00:06:07.650 --> 00:06:08.850
I'm back!

00:06:08.920 --> 00:06:10.460
Welcome back, Lucia.

00:06:10.460 --> 00:06:13.540
You're really late today. Where were you?

00:06:13.540 --> 00:06:14.820
Oh, hey.

00:06:15.200 --> 00:06:17.050
I should go and get changed.

00:06:28.210 --> 00:06:31.000
Come on! What's with you two?

00:06:31.000 --> 00:06:33.680
You're just staring at me!

00:06:34.020 --> 00:06:37.350
Oh, it's nothing. Was I really staring at you?

00:06:37.350 --> 00:06:40.110
You're just paranoid, Lucia.

00:06:40.400 --> 00:06:42.110
Is that so?

00:06:42.110 --> 00:06:48.400
Uhh, Lucia, have you ever been in love with two people at the same time?

00:06:48.580 --> 00:06:52.130
Eh? Why do you ask, all of a sudden?

00:06:52.130 --> 00:06:56.570
Oh no! Hypothetically speaking, of course.

00:06:56.570 --> 00:06:59.920
Yeah! Just hypothetically speaking, right?

00:07:01.320 --> 00:07:04.650
Well, hypothetically speaking, everyone's situation is different.

00:07:04.650 --> 00:07:06.650
Everyone's situation is different.

00:07:06.650 --> 00:07:10.310
So, Lucia, how do you feel about Rihito-san?

00:07:10.310 --> 00:07:14.340
Huh? How do I feel about Rihito-san?

00:07:14.340 --> 00:07:18.520
Yeah. We saw the two of you talking, and it looked like you were getting along well together.

00:07:19.640 --> 00:07:23.280
Why are you asking me this now?

00:07:24.990 --> 00:07:29.460
Ah, well we were just wondering, hypothetically, of course.

00:07:31.590 --> 00:07:35.690
If you were just speaking hypothetically, then nothing we were just talking about makes any sense.

00:07:35.690 --> 00:07:38.700
It's okay. You don't need to worry about it.

00:07:38.700 --> 00:07:40.640
Okay, if you say so.

00:07:41.150 --> 00:07:43.920
I guess it's better if I don't think about it any further.

00:07:43.950 --> 00:07:44.490
Eh?

00:07:44.650 --> 00:07:45.840
Lucia?

00:07:46.960 --> 00:07:49.940
My goodness, I feel tired.

00:07:49.940 --> 00:07:53.210
I see. You should probably go to bed early tonight.

00:07:53.210 --> 00:07:55.120
Yeah. You're right.

00:07:55.120 --> 00:07:59.060
If you take a bath and get a good night's rest, you'll definitely feel a lot better.

00:07:59.210 --> 00:08:00.880
Okay, I'll do that.

00:08:01.160 --> 00:08:02.150
Thank you.

00:08:02.910 --> 00:08:04.530
Good night, Lucia.

00:08:04.530 --> 00:08:05.940
Good night.

00:08:10.940 --> 00:08:14.890
I think Lucia's at her breaking point.

00:08:14.890 --> 00:08:19.380
She's probably getting tired of waiting for Kaito.

00:08:31.020 --> 00:08:34.350
Hey, Lucia! Could you help me carry something?

00:08:34.350 --> 00:08:36.200
Okay, be right there!

00:08:39.050 --> 00:08:42.670
Hey, Rina, how do you feel about what happened yesterday?

00:08:42.670 --> 00:08:44.380
What happened yesterday?

00:08:44.540 --> 00:08:47.040
Will Lucia develop feelings for Rihito-san?

00:08:47.040 --> 00:08:48.790
I don't really know.

00:08:48.790 --> 00:08:51.520
But I suppose it's not entirely out of the question.

00:08:51.990 --> 00:08:54.880
Rihito-san is a great guy.

00:08:54.990 --> 00:08:57.830
Lucia's just dense when it comes to people.

00:08:58.150 --> 00:09:01.250
I guess it's not that easy to change someone's feelings.

00:09:06.250 --> 00:09:08.360
Oww!

00:09:08.360 --> 00:09:10.780
Lucia is really dense.

00:09:10.780 --> 00:09:13.590
Yeah. She's completely useless.

00:09:20.000 --> 00:09:23.440
Uhh, can I have a fruit sandwich?

00:09:23.440 --> 00:09:26.310
Hey! Can I have a fruit sandwich!?

00:09:29.410 --> 00:09:35.030
But if Lucia's feelings towards Kaito don't change, does she have a chance?

00:09:35.030 --> 00:09:39.570
The problem is that Kaito is with Mikaru.

00:09:39.830 --> 00:09:43.860
It might be better if we encourage Lucia to try and go out with both Kaito and Rihito-san.

00:09:43.860 --> 00:09:50.240
If Lucia was capable of doing that, we wouldn't have to worry about her.

00:09:50.440 --> 00:09:51.950
That's true.

00:09:51.950 --> 00:09:55.780
Ahh! The fruit sandwiches are almost sold out!

00:10:01.290 --> 00:10:05.050
Aww, I ended up not being able to get a fruit sandwich.

00:10:05.050 --> 00:10:07.370
I ended up having to get a croquette roll instead.

00:10:08.490 --> 00:10:11.190
I really wanted a fruit sandwich!

00:10:12.500 --> 00:10:14.580
Dammit! I've had enough!

00:10:15.410 --> 00:10:17.420
What's wrong, Hanon?

00:10:17.420 --> 00:10:19.320
Why did you yell all of a sudden?

00:10:19.320 --> 00:10:22.590
I'm so tired of thinking about all of this!

00:10:22.590 --> 00:10:26.390
I don't use my brain much, and now I feel like I've overused it.

00:10:26.390 --> 00:10:27.200
Huh?

00:10:27.200 --> 00:10:31.670
At times like this, we should go sing our hearts out at a karaoke parlor!

00:10:31.850 --> 00:10:33.290
Karaoke?

00:10:37.480 --> 00:10:40.010
So which karaoke parlor should we go to?

00:10:40.250 --> 00:10:43.240
I don't really know much about karaoke, so I'll leave it to you, Hanon.

00:10:43.240 --> 00:10:46.950
Okay. Let's go try this "high tech" karaoke parlor.

00:10:53.530 --> 00:10:55.590
Hold it. Did you hear that just now?

00:10:56.010 --> 00:10:58.820
I think they were singing one of our songs.

00:10:58.820 --> 00:11:00.550
What in the world is going on?

00:11:01.410 --> 00:11:04.900
They came from this karaoke parlor.

00:11:04.900 --> 00:11:08.860
Why would our songs be in a karaoke machine?

00:11:08.860 --> 00:11:10.710
We should go and check it out.

00:11:56.480 --> 00:11:58.220
Yay!

00:11:58.220 --> 00:12:00.340
Eh? 40 points?

00:12:00.340 --> 00:12:03.570
Wait a minute! What's with this score?

00:12:03.570 --> 00:12:05.200
I think it's a bit low.

00:12:05.200 --> 00:12:09.270
I wonder, though. Why does this karaoke parlor have our songs?

00:12:09.270 --> 00:12:11.150
How should I know!?

00:12:11.150 --> 00:12:13.160
The more important problem is this score!

00:12:13.160 --> 00:12:16.100
This is my song! I won't stand for this!

00:12:16.100 --> 00:12:18.130
I'll get a high score on the next one!

00:12:18.130 --> 00:12:21.770
Hey, I think you've got your priorities mixed up.

00:12:21.770 --> 00:12:23.370
Wait a minute, Hanon.

00:12:23.370 --> 00:12:23.890
Here!

00:12:24.800 --> 00:12:27.360
Lucia! Rina! Come on!

00:12:52.190 --> 00:12:53.790
Eh? A group of three singing?

00:12:54.030 --> 00:12:57.050
Maybe they're the Mermaid Princesses?

00:13:07.090 --> 00:13:08.510
38 points...

00:13:08.510 --> 00:13:10.570
No. That's not possible.

00:13:10.570 --> 00:13:11.380
Why?

00:13:11.750 --> 00:13:16.550
That's such a low score. No way they're the Mermaid Princesses.

00:13:19.440 --> 00:13:22.090
What the heck? You should be angry about this, too!

00:13:23.000 --> 00:13:24.330
This is definitely strange.

00:13:24.330 --> 00:13:26.890
Is this machine broken?

00:13:26.890 --> 00:13:27.750
Rina.

00:13:27.750 --> 00:13:30.660
In any case, this score makes me mad!

00:13:30.660 --> 00:13:32.510
Yeah! I'm not going to stand for this!

00:13:32.510 --> 00:13:35.820
Okay! Let me try this time!

00:13:49.340 --> 00:13:50.850
Eh!?

00:13:50.850 --> 00:13:53.570
Lucia, leave the next one to me.

00:14:04.320 --> 00:14:06.260
No! That's not possible.

00:14:07.780 --> 00:14:08.800
Rina.

00:14:08.800 --> 00:14:11.730
It's bad when her score is lower than Lucia's.

00:14:11.730 --> 00:14:15.130
Okay! Let's do this!

00:14:21.590 --> 00:14:23.400
Green Pearl Voice!

00:14:26.080 --> 00:14:28.080
Aqua Pearl Voice!

00:14:30.790 --> 00:14:32.490
Pink Pearl Voice!

00:14:33.900 --> 00:14:35.930
If we don't get a high score...

00:14:35.930 --> 00:14:37.990
...we're going to complain to the manager!

00:14:37.990 --> 00:14:39.990
You don't have to go that far.

00:14:47.130 --> 00:14:50.900
Eh!? When{ the heck} did the Mermaid Princesses show up?

00:14:59.400 --> 00:15:04.410
I knew this bait would lure out the Mermaid Princesses!

00:15:04.450 --> 00:15:05.230
Lanhua!

00:15:05.230 --> 00:15:08.070
I get it. You set up this trap.

00:15:08.070 --> 00:15:10.010
You've realized that too late.

00:15:10.140 --> 00:15:13.340
I'll let you enjoy a nice song.

00:15:19.340 --> 00:15:21.030
She split apart again!

00:16:01.050 --> 00:16:02.110
Our bodies...

00:16:02.110 --> 00:16:02.840
...are moving...

00:16:02.840 --> 00:16:03.800
...against our will!

00:16:03.800 --> 00:16:07.810
I want to fly, fly across the vast skies again! Just once more!

00:16:08.130 --> 00:16:11.700
Huh? What was that? Hey, I don't understand!

00:16:11.930 --> 00:16:15.220
How true! We might be getting brainwashed!

00:16:59.970 --> 00:17:02.060
We're being{getting} brainwashed!

00:17:02.060 --> 00:17:04.100
Lucia-san! Hanon-san! Rina-san!

00:17:04.250 --> 00:17:06.040
You're not helping out Nikora-san back home!

00:17:06.070 --> 00:17:07.710
Why{ in the hell} are you at a karaoke parlor and...

00:17:07.710 --> 00:17:09.220
I don't know what's going on.

00:17:09.220 --> 00:17:11.620
What are you three doing?

00:17:11.620 --> 00:17:13.000
I don't know!

00:17:13.000 --> 00:17:14.780
Hippo! Help us!

00:17:14.950 --> 00:17:16.840
Alright.

00:17:21.010 --> 00:17:23.790
Ahh! It's a horse! It's a horse!

00:17:23.790 --> 00:17:25.790
What's going on?

00:17:25.790 --> 00:17:27.190
Help!

00:17:27.190 --> 00:17:29.370
Eh? The song stopped.

00:17:29.370 --> 00:17:30.930
Lucia! Hanon! Now!

00:17:30.930 --> 00:17:31.520
Okay!

00:17:31.520 --> 00:17:32.540
Got it!

00:18:25.440 --> 00:18:27.930
All right, let's go!

00:18:28.240 --> 00:18:31.420
Pichi Pichi Voice Live Start!

00:19:44.060 --> 00:19:45.900
I knew you'd do this!

00:19:45.900 --> 00:19:46.280
No!

00:19:46.280 --> 00:19:48.330
They're too strong!

00:19:48.670 --> 00:19:51.690
Love Shower Pitch!

00:19:55.680 --> 00:19:57.300
How about an encore?

00:19:57.300 --> 00:20:00.430
No one said anything about a horse coming here!

00:20:00.430 --> 00:20:03.500
That's it! I'm giving up on this!

00:20:03.940 --> 00:20:05.740
I'm not a horse!

00:20:09.170 --> 00:20:10.610
Huh?

00:20:10.610 --> 00:20:12.250
It disappeared.

00:20:12.250 --> 00:20:15.110
It was just an illusion that Lanhua created.

00:20:21.140 --> 00:20:22.160
Rihito-san!

00:20:22.330 --> 00:20:23.630
Hey, Lucia-chan.

00:20:23.630 --> 00:20:26.510
How about I take all of you out for a ride?

00:20:26.710 --> 00:20:28.400
Thank you, Rihito-san.

00:20:29.060 --> 00:20:30.770
I think we'll pass.

00:20:30.770 --> 00:20:32.320
Eh? Why?

00:20:32.320 --> 00:20:35.640
Rina and I have some errands to run.

00:20:35.640 --> 00:20:38.850
You and Rihito-san can go out for a ride.

00:20:44.430 --> 00:20:47.550
Lucia-chan, is there anywhere you want to go?

00:20:47.550 --> 00:20:50.350
Hmm. I don't know.

00:20:50.730 --> 00:20:53.370
I'd like to go someplace where the wind feels nice.

00:21:04.590 --> 00:21:08.210
The wind feels nice.

00:21:08.210 --> 00:21:11.650
I'm glad. You seem to be very cheerful.

00:21:11.650 --> 00:21:15.950
Yeah, Hanon and Rina are with me.  And...

00:21:15.950 --> 00:21:17.040
And?

00:21:17.590 --> 00:21:21.920
You were worried about me and comforted me.

00:21:23.450 --> 00:21:25.260
Thank you, Rihito-san!

00:21:25.520 --> 00:21:27.000
You're welcome.

00:21:27.490 --> 00:21:31.370
By the way, did you decide on what you'd like, Lucia-chan?

00:21:31.800 --> 00:21:35.230
Didn't I say that I was going to buy you a present?

00:21:35.230 --> 00:21:36.870
Have you thought about it?

00:21:39.760 --> 00:21:42.170
What's wrong, Lucia-chan?

00:21:43.550 --> 00:21:46.780
What I want is Kaito.

00:21:51.050 --> 00:21:54.800
The thing I want most is Kaito's heart.

00:21:57.060 --> 00:21:58.310
Lucia-chan.

00:21:58.840 --> 00:22:00.900
Kaito's heart...

00:23:51.050 --> 00:23:53.920
Are you having problems with love?

00:23:53.940 --> 00:23:54.570
Y-Yeah.

00:23:54.570 --> 00:23:57.570
Oh! I see that your love is full of obstacles.

00:23:57.570 --> 00:24:01.440
You need to throw your most treasured item into the ocean.

00:24:01.440 --> 00:24:03.190
My most treasured item?

00:24:03.190 --> 00:24:07.390
Yeah! You need to throw away the item that is the most precious to you.

00:24:07.390 --> 00:24:09.340
Something a girl treasures more than anything.

00:24:09.340 --> 00:24:11.680
If it can allow Kaito to remember...

00:24:12.000 --> 00:24:15.070
Next time on Mermaid Melody Pichi Pichi Pitch Pure:

00:24:15.070 --> 00:24:16.350
"Fortune of Love."

00:24:16.350 --> 00:24:19.210
If this can fulfill my desire, then I...
